{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788220329,"nonce":"YaYA9NNIcp/14rtawIPT12os+ng=","message":"Four merges in, four audits back, six agents still out.\n\n## Merged\n\n- `0c151c1` + `0dd1029` — step 0, the two mains converged and rebuilt.\n- `03398e4` — RUNLOG session 9.\n- `850c1eb` — DESIGN.md, the PawnSafe Class I entry.\n- `25f8ec6` — designate honesty (8b0b88f) + map-view alphabet identity (e6faa51).\n\n## THE AUDITS ALL PASSED, AND THE HEADLINE IS THAT THE CODE WAS THE STRONG PART\n\nAll four returned MERGEABLE WITH NAMED FIXES. Nothing is NOT MERGEABLE.\n\n**Both uncompiled branches COMPILE — 0 errors, 0 warnings, both of them.** 3.5's\nassembly carries all 18 new op strings; 3.6's carries all nine. That was the\nsingle largest unknown in this round and it is discharged.\n\n**3.6's scariest property turned out to be its safest.** It edits\nMedicalBillVerbs.cs, 3.4's shipped file, and the change is comment-only fixes\nplus a TRUE MOVE of RecipeAvailableNow into WorldSafe — character-identical body,\none added null guard that changes nothing, exactly one definition repo-wide, one\ncaller retargeted. accept/3.4-pawn-orders.py holds unchanged; no assertion flips.\nNo regression, and no duplication either.\n\n**3.5's NRE diagnosis was right and the branch already fixes it correctly**, on\nboth instances, by pre-empting rather than catching.\n\n**The DESIGN.md conflict this round was briefed on DOES NOT EXIST.** d180f57 is\nalready an ancestor of main and 3.5 appends at the tail; git 3-way merges them\nwith no conflict. Nor does the DESIGN.md owed-list: FIVE of its six items were\nalready paid by d180f57, and the list was written against the pre-merge file.\nAll five re-verified at source anyway. Only the Class I entry was outstanding.\n\n## WHAT THE AUDITS FOUND THAT NOBODY HAD FOUND, all of it in the SUITES and the PROSE\n\nThis is the round's lesson landing exactly where it was predicted to.\n\n- **3.5's suite has NINE structurally broken checks.** Nine call sites pass a\n  computed value where the $Env parameter belongs, shifting every later argument.\n  FOUR of them report PASS while asserting literally nothing; five are spurious\n  red. And 4.8g — the single most load-bearing check in the file, the proof that\n  un-wedging restored ticking — reads `data.ticks`, a key TimeDriver never emits.\n  It can only ever fail. Treat that suite's ~196 checks as ~187.\n- **4.2's auditor RAN here for the first time and passes its own selftest** — but\n  its advance-invariants check is PARTIALLY VACUOUS, demonstrated rather than\n  suspected: it reads only the DECLARED args, never the result's ticks_elapsed,\n  and TimeDriver defaults timeout_ticks to 600000 when `until` is set and the arg\n  is omitted — 10x the stated policy cap. A synthetic 5x violation reported PASS.\n- **A third verb trap, same shape as the two known ones.** PLAY-LOOP.md's act\n  list reads as though `orders` were an umbrella taking move-to/attack/rescue/\n  capture/tend as subcommands. It is a SIXTH, UNRELATED verb — and it is not\n  read-only: it can delete a bill, burns a scribed nextJobID per candidate, and\n  writes the scribed `paused` flag on every bill on the map.\n- **3.6's one real code defect: a PARTIAL MUTATION REPORTED AS `bad-args`.**\n  bill-add runs AddBill and THEN Configure, so a bad argument leaves the bill in\n  the stack — the agent reads bad-args, retries, and now has two bills.\n  storage-set throws inside its per-target loop after writing, so Act() is never\n  reached and there is NO JOURNAL ROW AT ALL: an unprovenanced state change,\n  which is the one thing Stamp/NoAction exist to prevent.\n- **3.5's .ps1 cannot run on this box even with pwsh installed** — $Root defaults\n  to $env:USERPROFILE and every path is built with a literal backslash.\n\n## Dispatched off the audits (audits report, orchestrator decides — Evan's rule)\n\nF1 (3.5 fixes, opus), F2 (4.2 fixes, sonnet), F3 (3.6 fixes + the acceptance\nsuite that does not exist, opus). Each carries its audit's findings as leads to\nVERIFY, not as gospel, and each is told that finding one of them wrong is a\nvaluable result.\n\n## Correction to the round's own brief, recorded\n\nRUNLOG sessions 7 and 8 were NOT unwritten — only session 9 was. And `bc2250b`,\nwhich the brief names among the four issues to close, DOES NOT EXIST in either\nbug store despite six merged commits citing it. Its work is on main regardless.","files":null}]}